A||||5||TheHans||problems with engine||||5||
Z||000000||TheHans||01-20-2001||02:01 PM||||Hey,<BR>I rebuilt my 85 2.5 sounds good but having some problems. <BR>It dies when I come off the interstate at the ramp. It likes to die when I put it in gear and I have to keep gassing it at stop signs. It gets horrible gas mileage. The integrator is at 80. It also idles at about 1900. (sometimes)<BR>EGR ?<BR>Bad Coil ?<BR>Any tests you guys could recommend?<BR>Thanks in advance. <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-20-2001||04:01 PM||||Check for error codes.<P>Incorrect timing<BR>malfunction in emission system<BR>Faulty EGR, PCV<BR>Faulty TAC vacuum motor or valve<BR>air leak into manifold vacuum<BR>faultydistributor rotor or cap<BR>improperly seated valves<BR>incorrect ignition wireing<BR>faulty ignition coil<P>When mine acted up, it was the timing.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Hank is Here||01-20-2001||05:04 PM||||My guess it the EGR or something of the like<BR>Also is it an auto or stick, could it possibly be a tcc?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||01-20-2001||08:10 PM||||I don't think the TC lockup would be the culprit if this is an auto. That doesn't account for the integrator or the idle.<P>I'd look at the stuff Lar said. timing, vacuum leaks, and such.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||01-20-2001||08:48 PM||||I would check timing or check out the distributor itself. Make sure the prongs are not bent and touching each other. I had the same problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheHans||01-20-2001||10:37 PM||||IT has a new distributer, rotor, plugs, and wires. New PCV too. <BR>TAC (refresh my memory)<BR>Haven't had the TCC hooked up for a while.<BR>I just set the timing. It may have slipped though. <BR>Hoped for, Searched, listened, sprayed, and measured vac., for a vac. leak none found.<BR>I was hoping it would be that easy.<BR>  TIMING---<BR>1. first cyl. @ TDC (comp. stroke)<BR>2. rotor to dist. post to plug<BR>3. fine tune and tighten<BR> Abbreviated but pretty close -eh<BR>Why is the word abbreviated so long?<P>Why do you say the valve seats <BR>OLD Lar?<BR>(Thanks everyone.)||||reg||1
